Break-then-fix: the four you'll actually hit

For each, the code that throws, the exact exception, and the fix — plus a test that proves the fix at 201 records.

1. SOQL in a loop → Too many SOQL queries: 101
apex
// ❌ BREAKS at record 101
public static void tagOpps_broken(List<Opportunity> opps) {
    for (Opportunity o : opps) {
        Account a = [SELECT Rating FROM Account WHERE Id = :o.AccountId];  // query per record
        o.Description = a.Rating;
    }
}

The query is inside the loop, so 200 records = 200 queries. It dies the instant the 101st runs — you never even reach record 200.

apex
// ✅ FIXED — 1 query regardless of volume
public static void tagOpps_fixed(List<Opportunity> opps) {

    Set<Id> acctIds = new Set<Id>();
    for (Opportunity o : opps) {
        if (o.AccountId != null) acctIds.add(o.AccountId);
    }
    if (acctIds.isEmpty()) return;

    Map<Id, Account> accts = new Map<Id, Account>([
        SELECT Rating FROM Account WHERE Id IN :acctIds
    ]);

    for (Opportunity o : opps) {
        Account a = accts.get(o.AccountId);
        if (a != null) o.Description = a.Rating;
    }
}

Collect keys → one query keyed by Id → O(1) lookups. Same instinct as killing an N+1.

*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

2. DML in a loop → Too many DML statements: 151
apex
// ❌ BREAKS at record 151
public static void createTasks_broken(List<Opportunity> opps) {
    for (Opportunity o : opps) {
        insert new Task(WhatId = o.Id, Subject = 'Follow up');  // 1 statement each
    }
}

Remember the statement-vs-row distinction: this is 200 statements. The fix turns it into 1 statement of 200 rows.

apex
// ✅ FIXED — 1 DML statement, 200 rows
public static void createTasks_fixed(List<Opportunity> opps) {
    List<Task> toInsert = new List<Task>();
    for (Opportunity o : opps) {
        toInsert.add(new Task(WhatId = o.Id, Subject = 'Follow up'));
    }
    if (!toInsert.isEmpty()) insert toInsert;
}

