3. Nested loop → Apex CPU time limit exceeded

This is the sneaky one — zero queries, zero DML, still dies. Bulkification-by-rote ("no SOQL in loops") doesn't catch it.

apex
// ❌ BREAKS — O(n²), ~40,000 iterations at 200×200, blows 10s CPU
public static void matchContacts_broken(List<Opportunity> opps, List<Contact> allContacts) {
    for (Opportunity o : opps) {
        for (Contact c : allContacts) {              // inner scan per outer record
            if (c.AccountId == o.AccountId) {
                o.Description = c.Email;
            }
        }
    }
}
apex
// ✅ FIXED — pre-index one side into a Map, O(n)
public static void matchContacts_fixed(List<Opportunity> opps, List<Contact> allContacts) {

    Map<Id, Contact> byAccount = new Map<Id, Contact>();
    for (Contact c : allContacts) {
        byAccount.put(c.AccountId, c);               // one pass to build the index
    }

    for (Opportunity o : opps) {
        Contact c = byAccount.get(o.AccountId);      // O(1) instead of a scan
        if (c != null) o.Description = c.Email;
    }
}

Two loops that run once each (n + n) instead of one loop inside another (n × n). The CPU limit counts Apex execution time, so collapsing the iteration count is the whole fix.

